    "editorial_content_WRzmHw": {
      "type": "editorial-content",
      "blocks": {
        "two_column_content_aUHVBW": {
          "type": "two_column_content",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Our Story",
            "show_heading_desktop": true,
            "show_heading_mobile": true,
            "text": "<p>A Shimus began with a familiar frustration. While working in New York, the founder struggled to find professional clothing that truly fit her petite frame. Jackets felt oversized, waistlines sat too low, proportions were always slightly off. Tailoring became routine. Compromise became expected. And over time, it became clear this wasn’t a personal problem - it was a design one.<br/><br/>Workwear simply wasn’t being created with scale in mind. A Shimus was founded to change that. From the very first pattern, every garment is designed specifically for petite proportions, with careful attention to balance, movement, and ease. Fit is never an adjustment or an afterthought, it’s the starting point. The result is workwear that feels natural the moment you put it on, allowing you to focus on your day rather than your clothes.<br/><br/>Craft is central to everything we do. A Shimus partners closely with skilled manufacturers in Japan, working across fabric development, tailoring, and construction. This small-batch, detail-driven approach reflects a deep respect for Japanese craftsmanship - where quality is built slowly, and longevity is the ultimate measure of value.<br/>Our collections are designed to live within real wardrobes. Tailored pieces that hold their shape. Silk dresses that move with ease. Separates that work together and wear well over time. Clothing that feels polished without being rigid, and refined without feeling precious.<br/><br/>At its core, A Shimus exists to support women navigating modern professional life. Not by telling them who to be, but by creating clothing that fits properly, lasts longer, and feels quietly confident in every setting.<br/><br/>A Shimus is not driven by trends. It is guided by intention, craftsmanship, and fit.<br/><br/>Workwear designed to fit.</p>",
            "enable_truncate_desktop": false,
            "truncate_lines_desktop": 3,
            "enable_truncate_mobile": true,
            "truncate_lines_mobile": 6,
            "show_read_more": true,
            "read_more_text": "Read More",
            "read_less_text": "Read Less"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "two_column_content_aUHVBW"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial Content",
      "settings": {
        "section_background_color": "#ffffff",
        "section_text_color": "#000000",
        "section_padding_top": 72,
